      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- File: `docs/schemas/rig.relay.audit_event.v1.schema.json` - Type: Draft 7 - Required fields (top-level): 6 - `$defs` are self-contained (definitions inlined from `receipt_envelope.v1` schema) - `additionalProperties: false` everywhere",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-16",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Supervisor Integration (P3b)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "The `RuntimeSupervisor` produces `AuditEvent` records from terminal execution events when configured with an ``audit_trail_store``.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-18",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- **Action**: ``EXECUTION_COMPLETED`` — one audit event per terminal event. - **Decision**: ``COMPLETED`` (exit code 0), ``FAILED`` (non-zero or timeout), ``REFUSED`` (blocked by lease/governance). - **Envelope**: Embedded `ReceiptEnvelope` with runtime invocation subject, execution request input, terminal output (hashes/bytes), and terminal event hash as evidence. - **Failure safety**: If audit append fails, a `RuntimeWarningEvent` is emitted and the terminal event is still delivered.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "See `docs/governance/runtime-supervisor.md` for constructor args and behavior.",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-20",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Related",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-21",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "- `rig_relay/evidence/receipt_envelope.py` — `ReceiptEnvelope`, `ReceiptActor`, `ReceiptSubject` models referenced by `AuditEvent` - `rig_relay/runtime/supervisor.py` — `RuntimeSupervisor` audit integration - `docs/schemas/rig.relay.audit_event.v1.schema.json` - `docs/governance/runtime-supervisor.md` - `tests/evidence/test_audit_trail.py` - `tests/runtime/test_runtime_supervisor.py` (see ``TestAuditIntegration``)",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "h2-22",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "Tamper Evidence",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard",
        "initially_visible": true
      }
    },
    {
      "block_id": "p-23",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "This store provides append-only JSONL persistence with best-effort fsync durability. It does **not** provide cryptographic tamper evidence. Hash-chain tamper evidence is designed separately — see [docs/governance/audit-trail-tamper-evidence.md](audit-trail-tamper-evidence.md).",
      "disclosure": {
        "level": "standard"
      }
    }
